  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In August 2023, the Iraqi government with ILO technical input, adopted the new Retirement and Social Security Law (No.18 of 2023) that represents a prominent step forward to enhancing social protection and achieving decent work in the country. As it has expanded the scope of social security systems and offered new benefits (unemployment and maternity insurance...) to cover previously excluded social groups such as workers in the informal economy and self-employed workers. 
This law forms a good opportunity to support the different workers organization to improve its representativeness, structures and a good opportunity to support the different workers&#x2019; organization to improve its representativeness and democratic structures. The ILO will continue working with the established Trade Union Coordination Committee to enhance the capacities of the different Iraqi national trade union centers to jointly organize workers in the informal economy by way of assisting in the implementation of the new law, with a view to restructure the union movement to better influence the socio-economic policies and laws mainly the draft trade union law.</narrative>
  </description>
